# SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075  -  CAT II
# The web server must only contain services and functions necessary for
# operation.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000075
group:           V-206375
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    Splunk can deactivate each service and function it ships - Splunk Web, the
                 KV Store, distributed search - and can set every installed app to a
                 declared enabled or disabled state, which is the product's equivalent of
                 deactivating a feature.

governs:         app.conf - Settings for an installed app: whether it is enabled, visible, and what it
                 may do.
governs:         distsearch.conf - How a search head reaches the indexers it searches.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           app.conf [install] state present
check:           server.conf [kvstore] disabled present
check:           distsearch.conf [distributedSearch] disabled present
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] startwebserver https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] startwebserver present
                 reason: "startwebserver = [0 | 1]. Set whether or not to start Splunk Web.
                         0 disables Splunk Web, 1 enables it. Default: 1"
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Which features and processes the deployment actually needs, which comes
                 from the deployment design; the product STIG marks a standalone
                 installation not applicable because all functions it provides are then
                 necessary.
external:        Services and packages installed on the host outside the application,
                 carried by the operating system build.

citation:        SPLK-CL-000300 fix text; app.conf.spec:124 (state = disabled | enabled,
                 default enabled), web.conf.spec:23, server.conf.spec:5234,
                 distsearch.conf.spec:36
finding:         The services and apps the application can deactivate are left at their
                 shipped defaults rather than declared, so the configuration does not show
                 that only the services and functions needed for operation are running.
